# Line-ending policy.
#
# `.editorconfig` has declared `end_of_line = lf` repo-wide since early on, but
# nothing enforced it: `core.autocrlf` is unset on the dev machines and there was
# no `.gitattributes`, so whatever each editor or script happened to write is
# what got committed. The result is a repo split roughly 226 CRLF files to 200
# LF, with eight files that are mixed *inside a single file* — including
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `backend/requirements-base.txt`.
#
# The practical cost is not aesthetic. A tool that rewrites a whole file in text
# mode flips every line, and a five-line change arrives as a 1800-line diff that
# no reviewer can read. That has already happened more than once.
#
# This file makes the working tree irrelevant: Git normalizes to LF in the
# object database on commit, so a file written with CRLF lands as LF and the
# diff shows only what actually changed.
#
# NOTE: adding this file does not rewrite existing history or the working tree.
# The 226 already-committed CRLF files stay as they are until someone runs
# `git add --renormalize .` in a dedicated commit. That is deliberately deferred
# until the open PRs land, because renormalizing 226 files while branches are in
# flight turns every one of them into a conflict.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts whose interpreter cares. A `.sh` with CRLF fails on Linux with the
# famously unhelpful `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, which matters because these
# run inside the Docker images.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# The Windows counterpart: `cmd.exe` needs CRLF in batch files.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diff, never normalize. Silent corruption otherwise.
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary

# Voice/model artefacts. None are tracked today, but this is a speech project
# with SoVITS checkpoints and reference audio one careless `git add` away, and
# the failure mode is a corrupted model that still loads.
*.wav           binary
*.mp3           binary
*.flac          binary
*.ogg           binary
*.opus          binary
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.onnx          binary
*.safetensors   binary
*.ckpt          binary
*.bin           binary
*.gguf          binary

# Lockfiles: generated, and reviewing them line by line is noise.
package-lock.json   -diff linguist-generated
Cargo.lock          -diff linguist-generated

# Better hunk headers when reading diffs in these languages.
*.py            diff=python
*.rs            diff=rust
*.md            diff=markdown
*.html          diff=html
*.css           diff=css
